<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · period</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sukkalmah period</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1970–1500 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century-bce">20th century BCE</a> · Also known as Sukkalmah system</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukkalmah">Sukkalmah</a> period was the era of Elamite history c. 1970–1500 BCE, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a> was ruled by grand regents called sukkalmahs. Succession passed between brothers before descending to the next generation. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-confederation">Elamite Confederation</a> profile treats it as a period when Elam was a major power in Mesopotamian affairs.</p></div>
